    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d303-a2">

                <pb facs="0598" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg502"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 473.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Earl of Derby to Mr.
                            Moran.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-03-26"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 26,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 17th instant, calling attention to the alleged neglect of
                    the authorities at Malta to check the conveyance of slaves on board British
                    vessels from Tripoli to Constantinople.</p>
                <p>I have not failed to communicate the contents of your note to the secretary of
                    state for the colonies, with a view to searching inquiries into the matter being
                    instituted at Malta; and as soon as the result of these inquiries is known I
                    shall have the honor of addressing a further communication to you on the
                    subject.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>DERBY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
